WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.440
In the next and final chapter chapter 8, we're going to talk about web frameworks.

00:05.440 --> 00:12.080
So web frameworks are a way for us to test and practice all of our new found Python knowledge.

00:12.080 --> 00:21.520
And build a very, very basic web application with unit tests using Python and the flask framework.

00:25.040 --> 00:27.360
Let's go through the basics of flask.

00:30.960 --> 00:35.920
There are a few different types of web frameworks in Python.

00:35.920 --> 00:38.080
Django is the very popular one.

00:38.080 --> 00:43.120
It's a fully featured high-level framework for building web apps.

00:43.120 --> 00:47.200
Django focuses on automating as much as possible.

00:47.200 --> 00:49.760
Many large scale sites run on Django.

00:49.760 --> 00:51.760
Instagram is one of them.

00:53.040 --> 00:59.120
Django started out as a CMS project, a content management system for a newspaper.

00:59.440 --> 01:02.880
And Django is a pretty heavy framework.

01:02.880 --> 01:08.560
It has a lot of opinions on how things should work and how things should be structured.

01:08.560 --> 01:12.400
If you want something lighter-weight, flask is a good choice.

01:13.200 --> 01:16.000
Flask is a micro framework for Python.

01:16.000 --> 01:23.120
And it allows users to make pretty basic back-end APIs and web apps with a minimum amount of code.

01:23.760 --> 01:26.080
Flask is a little bit easier for beginners.

01:26.080 --> 01:28.000
It's not quite as opinionated.

01:28.000 --> 01:31.360
There are less set-up steps, less requirements.

01:31.360 --> 01:34.880
So that's when I'm going to be focusing on for today's exercises.

01:34.880 --> 01:40.400
But don't think that flask is a simple web framework.

01:40.400 --> 01:44.000
The great thing about flask is as your web application grows,

01:44.000 --> 01:48.000
you can add on all sorts of different modules to help you

01:49.920 --> 01:56.000
add on functionality for databases or other types of things that your web application might

01:56.160 --> 01:56.720
want to do.

01:58.720 --> 02:03.120
Yeah, another web framework that you might hear of or see as pyramid.

02:03.920 --> 02:07.600
It's a fast and it's an advanced framework.

02:07.600 --> 02:10.400
It's a successor to the older pylons framework.

02:12.000 --> 02:18.960
So still popular and used, but not quite as popular for new projects.

02:18.960 --> 02:21.840
Pyramid is open source and also actively developed.

